      en: "The Bromo Tengger Semeru National Park in East Java is home to one of the most spectacular volcanic landscapes in the world. Spanning approximately 500 square kilometers, it is dominated by the massive Tengger Caldera, inside of which rises the famous Mount Bromo (2,329 m). Another striking feature is the 'Sea of Sand' (Laut Pasir), a vast plain of volcanic ash surrounding the peaks. To the south of the park towers Mount Semeru, which at 3,676 meters is the highest mountain in Java and one of the country's most active volcanoes. The region is not only geologically significant but also the cultural home of the Tenggerese people, a Hindu minority who celebrate the annual Yadnya Kasada festival. During this ceremony, devotees bring offerings to the edge of Bromo's crater to appease the gods. The park is a major destination for mountaineers and trekkers, who primarily come to witness the sunrise over the bizarre, lunar-like landscape. Its biodiversity includes subalpine forests and rare orchid species that thrive in the cooler highland air.",
      es: "El Parque Nacional Bromo-Tengger-Semeru en Java Oriental concentra un paisaje que parece más un boceto geológico que una región vacacional. En el centro se encuentra la caldera de Tengger, de unos 10 kilómetros de ancho, con su mar de arena, del que emergen el Bromo y otros conos. Al sur domina el monte Semeru, de 3.676 metros, la cima más alta de Java y uno de los volcanes más activos del país. Entre cenizas, aire frío matutino y rituales hinduistas de los Tenggerese, el parque muestra cuán estrechamente están vinculadas la naturaleza y la cultura en el este de Java. Geografía K7 – Calderas volcánicas y el Cinturón de Fuego del Pacífico.",
